    LLM: 'Game: Vira. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Vira is Sweden's historic national card game (19th century). 3-4 players (3 active). 52-card deck. 13 each + 13-card talon. Complex bidding with ~40 contract types. KÃ¶pspel (buy from talon), Solospel (no talon), Gaskspel (take all talon). Declarer vs 2 defenders. Scoring via 'virapulla' (token pot).",
    objective: 'The highest bidder becomes the declarer and plays alone against the other two. The declarer must either take at least a stated number of tricks or, in misery contracts, lose every trick; the defenders try to prevent the declarer from making the contract.',
